  "notes": "Inglewood’s **live band as production unit** — a session-musician collective, and the most harmonically complete entry in this section. Every parameter follows from the personnel: two keyboard players give real functional harmony (maj7, m9, 13ths, passing diminished, `ii–V–I` cycles and key changes between sections); a **live drummer** means ghost notes, rimshots, hi-hat barks and high velocity variance with timing loose against the grid; **live electric bass** walks across E1–C3 with no glides; and a staff top-line writer means the countermelody is a real instrumental part rather than a fill. ⚠ `medium`: personnel and instrumentation are documented, tempo habits inferred from the catalogue. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
